      "description": "Watch CSKA Sofia vs Maccabi Tel Aviv highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 13, 2026. The stage was set for a compelling UEFA Europa League encounter as CSKA Sofia hosted Maccabi Tel Aviv on August 13, 2026 . Both sides entered the pitch with everything to play for in a match that promised high energy and tactical drama. Maccabi Seize the Initiative From the opening whistle, the visiting side looked sharp, looking to exploit spaces in the Bulgarian defense. The breakthrough came early in the 12th minute when Osher Davida delivered a pinpoint assist to Dor Peretz , who clinicaly finished to give Maccabi Tel Aviv the lead. The goal sparked a physical battle in the midfield, leading to several cautions. CSKA Sofia 's Bruno Jordao was booked in the 26th minute, followed shortly by the goalscorer Dor Peretz , as both teams fought tooth and nail for control of the tempo. A Second-Half Rollercoaster The second half began with tactical adjustments, as James Eto'o replaced Bruno Jordao for the hosts. Despite the change, it was Maccabi Tel Aviv who struck again. In the 61st minute, Osher Davida turned provider once more, setting up Ester Sokler for a composed finish to double the advantage. However, CSKA Sofia refused to go down without a fight. In the 66th minute, James Eto'o made an immediate impact by assisting Stefano Sensi , who found the back of the net to reduce the deficit. The momentum seemed to be shifting until disaster struck for the hosts just three minutes later. In the 69th minute, a defensive mishap led to an own goal by Fedor Lapoukhov , handing the visitors a two-goal cushion and deflating the home crowd's spirits. Late Drama and Disciplined Defense As the clock wound down, the match became increasingly fractured. A flurry of yellow cards followed, with Issouf Sissokho , Elad Madmon , and Max Ebong all entering the referee's book. Substitutions from both managers attempted to alter the flow, but Maccabi Tel Aviv remained disciplined at the back. Despite the late pressure from the home side, the visitors held firm to secure a significant victory on the European stage, leaving CSKA Sofia to reflect on a night of missed opportunities and defensive errors."
